# wellnessmedcare.com - build-time settings
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local builds, or set the same variables in your
# hosting platform's environment settings (Netlify: Site configuration >
# Environment variables; Cloudflare Pages: Settings > Variables) and redeploy.
#
# IMPORTANT: this is a fully static site, so these are read at BUILD time, not at
# request time. Changing a value requires a rebuild/redeploy to take effect.
# The PUBLIC_ prefix means the value is embedded in the shipped HTML/JS - never
# put a secret in a PUBLIC_ variable. Nothing in this file is a secret.
#
# Every variable is optional. With all of them unset the site builds and runs
# with analytics off and the newsletter form hidden.

# --- Analytics (pick one, or neither) ---------------------------------------

# Google Analytics 4 measurement ID. The site's own property (G-0LT2L2MLY3) is
# built in as the default via src/site-config.ts, so leave this UNSET for normal
# builds. Set it to a different ID to use another property, or to an empty value
# (PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=) to disable GA entirely, e.g. for a staging build.
# GA is consent-gated either way: the banner appears automatically and NO request
# is made to Google until the visitor accepts. Declining is remembered per
# device; visitors can change their choice on the privacy policy page.
#PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# GoatCounter code, e.g. "wellnessmedcare" for wellnessmedcare.goatcounter.com
# (free account at goatcounter.com). Cookieless, no personal data, so no
# consent banner is needed or shown. Fine to run alongside GA.
PUBLIC_GOATCOUNTER_CODE=

# --- Newsletter --------------------------------------------------------------

# Your email provider's form POST endpoint (Buttondown, ConvertKit, Formspree,
# MailerLite...). While empty, the signup form does not render anywhere -
# deliberately, so the site never ships a form that silently drops addresses.
# Example (Buttondown): https://buttondown.com/api/emails/embed-subscribe/yourlist
PUBLIC_NEWSLETTER_ENDPOINT=

# --- Production server (npm run start only) ----------------------------------

# Port for scripts/serve.mjs when self-hosting the built site on a Node host.
# CDN platforms (Netlify, Cloudflare Pages) ignore this. Runtime, not build-time.
PORT=8080
